     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Answer to a question about partial vs. complete sample of living species in a BioGeoBEARS analysis...<div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Nick</div><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">---------- Forwarded message ----------<br>\r\nFrom: <b class=\"gmail_sendername\">Jack D</b> <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ja...@ces.iisc.ernet.in</a>&gt;</span><br>Date: Wed, Sep 3, 2014 at 3:13 AM<br>Subject: Re: Data type used in BioGeoBEARS<br>\r\nTo: Nick Matzke &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mat...@berkeley.edu</a>&gt;<br><br><br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\">Ahoy!</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\">Thanks a lot for the reply.  I shall keep them in mind when running my analysis.  Sure, you may post this question and answer on the listserv.  Thanks!</span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\">Cheers.</span></div><br><br><div href=\"http://WISESTAMP_SIG_gmail_session\"><div style=\"font-size:13px;font-family:Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px 0px 8px\"><p style=\"margin:0px\"></p><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Divya B.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Research scholar</span><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Karanth Lab</span><br></div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Center for Ecological Sciences (CES)</span><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Indian Institute of Science (IISc)</span><br><span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Ph: 9916363257</span><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">e-mail: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ja...@ces.iisc.ernet.in</a> </span><p></p>\r\n<div style=\"clear:both\"></div></div>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/-7z7Iyd_u71mwZZlgu5pVoIu7wXyj1q9V_5kFAVPfpeky7ek61bGW9kGlscDHZYooyaxknzNDVCpMmikfKitGCYeW5gpqAcWpCJJXpmiYayT4MWOUygiv2CZyAj82pgMrMeFcVe_JHvExNt82qRiaAE=s0-d-e1-ft#https://wisestamp.appspot.com/pixview.gif?p=chrome&amp;v=3.44.0&amp;t=1409728396018&amp;u=e494ec730c4ca423\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>\r\n<div>On Wed, Sep 3, 2014 at 9:19 AM, Nick Matzke <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mat...@berkeley.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br>\r\n</div><div>You can run it with a partial phylogeny.  Your results will be better with a full phylogeny, but of course even a complete phylogeny will be missing all of the extinct groups.  BioGeoBEARS is a form of ancestral state estimation applied to biogeography (a special kind of character state), so the logic about phylogenetic diversity analyses isn&#39;t really applicable.  Basically, you want as much data as you can practically gather to get the best results, but of course all studies are limited by what is available.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>My 2014 SysBio paper has a big section simulating the effect of missing extinct species, basically it doesn&#39;t hurt ancestral range estimation too much as long as the rates of change are low.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<br></div><div>Can I post this answer to the BioGeoBEARS listserv so that others with similar questions may benefit?</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Nick</div><div><br></div></div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div><div><div><div>On Tue, Aug 26, 2014 at 6:05 AM, Jack D <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ja...@ces.iisc.ernet.in</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div>\r\n\r\n</div></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\">Hello there,</span></div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\">I am doing my Ph.D. on the phylogenetic perspective of the biogeography of Western Ghats flora.  I am currently formulating my work and the first step is to do phylogenetic diversity analysis.  For the next step I wanted to analyse it using the BioGeoBEARS tools and would like to know what kind of data and phylogeny is required for it.  Should it be a complete phylogeny of all known species (across the globe) that include the species in my study area or can I also effectively work on pruned phylogenies (as is done with phylogenetic diversity calculations) that include the phylogeny of only the species in my study area?  I ask, because I plan to look at all tree species from the whole of Angiosperms and it is not possible to do the whole Angiosperm phylogeny (of all species across the globe) for this study.  Thanks very much!</span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"background-color:rgb(207,226,243)\">Cheers!</span></div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(102,0,0)\"><br></div></div></div></div></div><div href=\"http://WISESTAMP_SIG_gmail_session\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-size:13px;font-family:Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div><div><div><div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 8px\"><p style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Divya B.</span><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Research scholar</span><br><span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Karanth Lab</span><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Centre for Ecological Sciences</span><br><span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Indian Institute of Science</span><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">Ph: 9916363257</span><br><span style=\"font-family:&#39;comic sans ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,128,128);background-color:rgb(204,255,255)\">e-mail: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ja...@ces.iisc.ernet.in</a></span> </p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"clear:both\"></div></div></div></div></div></div><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/0fj21VnK6SEOcL3fKwkdI78p3x3UCOat96NVf9bbIlNGQY4BBVGkBueDvHZS--W2rn1my4Dq4_SnGKu7RscQfF9_grEltrCP-ghy6cxtU1FnHQ=s0-d-e1-ft#http://www.sng.ecs.soton.ac.uk/mailscanner/images/1x1spacer.gif\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" alt=\"Web Bug from https://wisestamp.appspot.com/pixview.gif?p=chrome&amp;v=3.44.0&amp;t=1409058212419&amp;u=38b3ba590c4ca423\"></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n<br>-- \r\n<br>This message has been scanned for viruses and\r\n<br>dangerous content by\r\n<a href=\"http://www.mailscanner.info/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.mailscanner.info/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485495670000&amp;usg=AOvVaw30cYAHrSqt7ezK_Q7p4XJh\"><b>MailScanner</b></a>, and is\r\n<br>believed to be clean.\r\n\r\n</font></span></font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</div><br></div></div>\r\n"
